.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt IS-DOCKED 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm is-docked
.Nd tell whether this laptop sits in its dock
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl qv
.Nm
.Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
tells whether a laptop sits in its dock.
A USB-C dock does not announce itself, so docked is inferred from three
things a dock provides at once, and means all three: external power, a
USB network interface (the dock's), and a connected external screen,
one that is not an internal panel
.Pq eDP, LVDS or DSI .
.Nm
prints
.Ql docked=acline,if-usb,screen
and exits 0 when all three are met, and
.Ql undocked
and exits 1 otherwise.
.Pp
Each criterion is read where the system keeps it.
On
.Fx :
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
power is the
.Va hw.acpi.acline
sysctl;
.It
the network interface is any
.Xr ue 4
interface, which every USB ethernet driver attaches as;
.It
the screens are the connectors drm-kmod lists as
.Va sys.class.drm.card Ns Ar N Ns Va - Ns Ar connector Ns Va .status
sysctls, or, without them, what
.Xr xrandr 1
reports under X.
Without either, the screen cannot be checked, which is said on stderr,
and counts as no screen.
.El
.Pp
On Linux, from sysfs alone:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
power is a supply of type Mains or USB that is online under
.Pa /sys/class/power_supply ,
a USB supply counting because a USB-C dock powers the laptop over USB;
.It
the network interface is one under
.Pa /sys/class/net
whose device sits on USB, Wi-Fi interfaces excepted;
.It
the screens are the connectors under
.Pa /sys/class/drm .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h
Print the usage and exit.
.It Fl q
Quiet: print nothing, and answer with the exit status only.
.It Fl v
Say on stderr, for each criterion, whether it was met and by what: the
supply, the interface, the connector.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev DISPLAY
On
.Fx
without drm-kmod connectors,
.Xr xrandr 1
is asked only when it is set.
.It Ev SYSFS
The root of sysfs on Linux, instead of
.Pa /sys .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Docked.
.It 1
Not docked, or the platform is neither
.Fx
nor Linux.
.It 2
A usage error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Turn the internal panel off when the laptop is docked:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ is-docked -q && screen-extend -p off
.Ed
.Pp
See which criterion is missing:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ is-docked -v
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr screen-extend 1 ,
.Xr xrandr 1 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh CAVEATS
The dock is recognised by what it provides, not by what it is: any USB
network interface counts, and a dock whose network interface is PCIe
over Thunderbolt does not.
.Pp
.Xr acpi_dock 4
is not consulted: it covers ACPI docking stations, not USB-C docks.
